{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_19-20-29-omnipaxos-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('update.json'))\ne=d['experiment']\nd['rationale']=\\\"Ninth turn: the per-case endpoint names made the contrast measurable (CheckRun a7083e51d44b4b1589eeb21b40848782: non-snapshot case violated, snapshot case holds), and the same harness is now extended with the gap's other half: the captured persistent (RocksDB) backend under the identical request. Run locally first, that third case also aborts, but at a different site - the panic message is 'Error reading from storage.: ErrHelper' raised inside the core crate at omnipaxos/src/sequence_paxos/mod.rs:428 (create_log_sync's expect), not the in-memory arithmetic panic, because PersistentStorage::get_suffix returns an error for a request below its compacted prefix instead of the empty suffix its trait specifies. Submitted as a further revision of the same experiment so both halves of the applicability gap are measured.\\\"\ne['previous_id']='630a5737b8394c66a425abf9045414c5-experiment'\ne['revision_reason']=\\\"Third case added for the gap's second half: the identical request is now also exercised against the captured persistent storage backend, with its own endpoint event name (log_sync_outcome_persistent) and its own state admission.\\\"\ne['scope']['description']=\\\"Three scenarios in one test, each driving one responder replica through a legal leader prefix (Prepare, AcceptSync with six entries and decided_idx 6, forwarded Compaction::Trim(6)) and then a legal Prepare with decided_idx 3 and an older accepted round: (a) snapshots disabled with the in-memory backend, (b) snapshots enabled with the in-memory backend, (c) snapshots disabled with the persistent RocksDB backend. The outcome of handling that Prepare is reported per case.\\\"\ne['scope']['assumptions'].append(\\\"For case (c) the responder uses PersistentStorage opened on a fresh temporary directory, with the same entry type as case (a); the temporary directory is kept alive for the case and dropped afterwards.\\\")\ne['scope']['assumptions'].append(\\\"Cases (a) and (b) use the in-memory backend behind a shared handle so the same code path is exercised with and without snapshots.\\\")\ne['scope']['excluded'].append(\\\"Behaviour when overflow checks are disabled (release profile) is not measured for any case.\\\")\ne['scope']['parameters']['cases']=[\\\"nosnapshot_entry\\\",\\\"snapshot_entry\\\",\\\"persistent_backend_entry\\\"]\ne['prefix']=\\\"scenario(case, snapshots, outcome_event, store, mk) builds one OmniPaxos instance (pid 2, nodes 1,2,3) over the supplied storage and then calls, in order: handle_incoming(Prepare{n: (1,1,pid 1), decided_idx: 0, n_accepted: 0, accepted_idx: 0}); handle_incoming(AcceptSync{n: (1,1,pid 1), seq_num: (session 0, counter 1), decided_idx: 6, log_sync: {decided_snapshot: None, suffix: six entries 0..5, sync_idx: 0, stopsign: None}}); handle_incoming(Compaction::Trim(6)). It then emits case_started and state_reached (both carrying case and use_snapshots, plus accepted_idx/decided_idx/compacted_idx on state_reached), and finally calls handle_incoming(Prepare{n: (1,2,pid 1), decided_idx: 3, n_accepted: 0, accepted_idx: 6}) inside catch_unwind, emitting the case-specific outcome event with case, use_snapshots, outcome, panic message and the three indices. The test runs the prefix three times: 'nosnapshot_entry' (UseSnapshots false, in-memory backend, event log_sync_outcome_nosnapshot), 'snapshot_entry' (UseSnapshots true, in-memory backend, event log_sync_outcome_snapshot) and 'persistent_backend_entry' (UseSnapshots false, PersistentStorage opened on a fresh tempdir, event log_sync_outcome_persistent).\\\"\ne['responsibility']=\\\"The three cases separate which captured component decides the outcome: the core's log-update construction selects its branch from T::Snapshot::use_snapshots() and the deciding node's decided index; with the in-memory backend the abort is raised by its unchecked subtraction inside MemoryStorage::get_suffix, and with the persistent backend the storage returns an error for the same request and the core's own expect in create_log_sync raises the abort.\\\"\ne['prerequisites'].append({\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admitted_persistent\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"state_reached\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"case\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"persistent_backend_entry\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"use_snapshots\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"accepted_idx\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":6},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"decided_idx\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":6},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"compacted_idx\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":6}]})\ne['comparisons'].append({\\\"event\\\":\\\"log_sync_outcome_persistent\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"case\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admitted_persistent\\\",\\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"outcome\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"completed\\\"},\\\"description\\\":\\\"With the captured persistent backend and no snapshots, handling the stale node's Prepare completes instead of aborting.\\\"})\njson.dump(d, open('update.json','w'), indent=2)\nprint(len(e['comparisons']), 'comparisons')\nEOF\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_19-20-29-omnipaxos-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
